WEBVTT

00:00:01.580 --> 00:00:06.140
Vice President, about the second-term budget
committee report I asked you to compile yesterday...

00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:08.150
Oh, it's already done.

00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:09.670
What? Already?

00:00:09.670 --> 00:00:10.570
Here you go.

00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:11.400
Thanks.

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:15.590
Vice President, have you made a list of clubs 
requesting stalls at the school festival?

00:00:15.590 --> 00:00:16.680
It's already done.

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:17.410
I see.

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:19.280
<b>PSO2</b> Report
<b>Tachibana Itsuki</b>

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:19.740
Here's my report.

00:00:20.610 --> 00:00:21.910
Good work.

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:22.900
Vice President.

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:23.500
Yes?

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:24.840
Have you—

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:24.840
What about—

00:00:25.610 --> 00:00:26.720
Go ahead.

00:00:27.010 --> 00:00:30.500
What about next Monday's school 
festival committee meeting?

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:31.850
I've already let them know.

00:00:31.850 --> 00:00:34.120
Have you collected the 
cafeteria's surveys?

00:00:34.390 --> 00:00:36.350
I'll pick them up after school today.

00:00:36.350 --> 00:00:37.010
Thanks.

00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:41.020
Here are the application 
forms you requested.

00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:42.700
Thanks.

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:43.970
You're welcome.

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:45.520
See you after school.

00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:49.890
This is pretty well written.

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:51.230
Indeed.

00:00:51.230 --> 00:00:54.310
President, he might be a great find after all.

00:00:54.310 --> 00:00:55.160
You think so?

00:00:55.160 --> 00:00:57.530
As usual, you've got a keen eye.

00:00:57.980 --> 00:00:59.440
You're exaggerating.

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:05.690
<i>"Facing a side of myself that
 I didn't know existed has been</i>

00:01:05.690 --> 00:01:07.600
<i>my biggest discovery playing </i>PSO2.<i>"</i>

00:01:08.610 --> 00:01:11.710
<i>His sense for the game 
seems relatively high.</i>

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:17.470
<i>But his play is overenthusiastic.</i>

00:02:50.850 --> 00:02:54.360
<b>Quest 02       The Aloof Warrior</b>

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:53.520
Take your seats, class.

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:55.420
Let me introduce our 
transfer student.

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:00.550
Suzuki Aika.

00:03:00.550 --> 00:03:03.060
I've been assigned to this 
class starting today.

00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:03.990
Nice to meet you.

00:03:03.990 --> 00:03:05.450
"Assigned"?

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:06.740
She's cute.

00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:10.140
Suzuki-san has been living overseas

00:03:10.140 --> 00:03:12.720
and just returned to 
Japan the other day.

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:14.600
Why don't you give a 
simple introduction?

00:03:14.600 --> 00:03:16.750
You want me to present my background?

00:03:16.750 --> 00:03:17.500
What?

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:19.760
Uh, yeah. Your background.

00:03:20.440 --> 00:03:24.200
Due to my parents being 
artists based overseas,

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:27.260
I've spent most of my life since 
grade school living abroad.

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:30.330
Since my childhood, 
I've enjoyed physical activity.

00:03:30.330 --> 00:03:31.470
I demonstrated exceptional talent

00:03:31.470 --> 00:03:35.750
in the fields of leg strength 
and swimming at a young age,

00:03:35.750 --> 00:03:38.440
often gaining me the admiration 
of those around me.

00:03:38.730 --> 00:03:41.500
Because I attended an international 
school while living abroad,

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:44.310
It sounds like she's describing 
a character's backstory.

00:03:41.500 --> 00:03:43.010
in addition to Japanese,

00:03:43.010 --> 00:03:45.120
my mother tongue, I'm familiar
 with several languages.

00:03:44.590 --> 00:03:45.910
She's cute.

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:47.660
That's all.

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:48.720
Uh, okay.

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:52.540
You can sit in that 
empty seat in the back.

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:53.420
Okay.

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:55.860
Tachibana, show her 
around the academy.

00:03:55.860 --> 00:03:57.220
Got it.

00:04:00.220 --> 00:04:01.220
Nice to meet you.

00:04:01.220 --> 00:04:02.190
Nice to meet you.

00:04:06.220 --> 00:04:07.300
Is something wrong?

00:04:07.300 --> 00:04:09.150
Oh, no.

00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:11.560
Am I tired?

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:13.560
Your parents are artists? 
What do they do?

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:14.360
Are they painters?

00:04:14.360 --> 00:04:15.200
Musicians?

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:16.390
More or less.

00:04:16.390 --> 00:04:18.260
How do you feel about 
lesbian relationships?

00:04:18.260 --> 00:04:20.160
They are what they are.

00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:22.190
Where'd you get your hair done?

00:04:22.190 --> 00:04:22.880
It's natural.

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:24.150
Do you have any hobbies?

00:04:24.150 --> 00:04:26.620
Do I have to answer that question?

00:04:26.940 --> 00:04:29.870
What? No, you don't <i>have</i> to...

00:04:31.340 --> 00:04:33.020
Itsuki, where are you going?

00:04:33.020 --> 00:04:33.620
The bathroom.

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:37.570
Excuse me.

00:04:45.160 --> 00:04:47.390
Height: 173 centimeters.

00:04:47.390 --> 00:04:49.060
Weight: 62 kilograms.

00:04:49.060 --> 00:04:50.740
Estimated inclination 
during acceleration...

00:04:50.740 --> 00:04:51.390
What?

00:04:52.120 --> 00:04:53.230
Don't mind me.

00:04:53.230 --> 00:04:54.260
Okay.

00:04:56.270 --> 00:04:57.770
<b>Men's Bathroom</b>

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:06.900
What do you want?

00:05:07.180 --> 00:05:08.280
Don't mind me.

00:05:10.340 --> 00:05:11.780
I told you not to mind me.

00:05:11.780 --> 00:05:14.000
Well, I do. I do mind you.

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:17.550
Suzuki-san, men's and women's bathrooms
 are separate here in Japan.

00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:19.610
And the girls' bathroom is over here.

00:05:19.900 --> 00:05:20.790
I see.

00:05:21.090 --> 00:05:22.330
There she is.

00:05:22.330 --> 00:05:23.550
Suzuki-san!

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:36.880
My apologies.

00:05:36.880 --> 00:05:37.730
It's okay.

00:05:38.050 --> 00:05:39.470
I'm going to the bathroom, too.

00:05:40.730 --> 00:05:54.370
Women's
Bathroom

00:05:41.330 --> 00:05:42.610
That was amazing.

00:05:42.840 --> 00:05:44.540
You were amazing, too.

00:05:44.540 --> 00:05:47.160
I'm surprised you could 
keep up with her.

00:05:47.160 --> 00:05:48.170
You've got it all wrong.

00:05:48.170 --> 00:05:50.280
She matched the speed of my block.

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:51.010
What?

00:05:51.010 --> 00:05:53.400
Returning kids are to be feared.

00:05:55.870 --> 00:06:00.000
School Festival After-Party

00:05:55.870 --> 00:06:00.000
◦ Folk Dance

00:05:55.870 --> 00:06:00.000
◦ Karaoke Contest

00:05:55.870 --> 00:06:00.000
◦ Ask Your Crush Out

00:05:55.870 --> 00:06:00.000
◦ Cross-dressing Pageant

00:05:56.440 --> 00:06:00.000
This concludes today's topics.

00:06:00.290 --> 00:06:01.560
Good work today.

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:03.000
Good work.

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:07.010
Vice President, take the post-meeting 
report to the faculty office.

00:06:07.470 --> 00:06:08.500
Got it.

00:06:08.500 --> 00:06:09.680
Tachibana-kun.

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:10.530
Yes?

00:06:10.530 --> 00:06:12.260
This is well written.

00:06:12.260 --> 00:06:13.310
Isn't it?

00:06:13.310 --> 00:06:16.390
But you're just enjoying yourself.

00:06:16.390 --> 00:06:20.020
This doesn't describe what kind of 
game <i>PSO2</i> is or its significance.

00:06:20.710 --> 00:06:22.270
Try to include those in the future.

00:06:22.270 --> 00:06:23.620
Piece of cake.

00:06:23.900 --> 00:06:26.750
I'm off to become an 
ARKS again tonight.

00:06:26.750 --> 00:06:28.290
Excuse me.

00:06:30.650 --> 00:06:31.680
He's flippant.

00:06:31.680 --> 00:06:33.300
Easily flattered.

00:06:33.300 --> 00:06:34.320
On top of that...

00:06:34.320 --> 00:06:35.880
He's simple-minded.

00:06:35.880 --> 00:06:37.160
Y-Yeah.

00:07:03.920 --> 00:07:05.660
Don't shout so carelessly.

00:07:05.660 --> 00:07:08.180
S-Suzuki-san, are you going home?

00:07:08.180 --> 00:07:08.940
Yes.

00:07:08.940 --> 00:07:11.190
Then let's go to the dorm together.

00:07:11.190 --> 00:07:11.910
Okay.

00:07:12.470 --> 00:07:13.800
How long have you been in the dorm?

00:07:13.800 --> 00:07:15.660
I just reported in yesterday.

00:07:15.940 --> 00:07:17.110
"Reported in"?

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:20.410
<b>Seiga Academy Student Dormitory</b>

00:07:17.110 --> 00:07:20.410
Whatever. I'll show 
you around the dorm.

00:07:20.410 --> 00:07:21.760
I appreciate it.

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:24.380
Do all the students live here?

00:07:24.380 --> 00:07:27.480
What? You didn't know this 
is a boarding school?

00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:30.040
Of course I know.

00:07:32.320 --> 00:07:34.620
Welcome back, kids.

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:35.820
Good work today.

00:07:35.820 --> 00:07:37.560
Well done on your mission.

00:07:38.960 --> 00:07:41.700
Once you enter the dorm, 
the girls' building is to the right,

00:07:41.700 --> 00:07:43.230
and the boys' is to the left.

00:07:43.230 --> 00:07:43.940
I see.

00:07:43.940 --> 00:07:48.190
I can't enter the girls' building, 
so I'll show you the communal spaces.

00:07:48.530 --> 00:07:50.280
This is the free room.

00:07:50.840 --> 00:07:52.530
You can use it until nine.

00:07:52.990 --> 00:07:56.400
There are libraries, audiovisual rooms,

00:07:56.400 --> 00:07:58.360
and free spaces all around the place,

00:07:58.360 --> 00:08:00.160
so feel free to use them.

00:08:00.730 --> 00:08:02.410
Boys and girls eat their meals
 at the same time.

00:08:02.850 --> 00:08:05.430
There are bathrooms and laundry 
rooms in each building,

00:08:05.430 --> 00:08:08.340
and there are washing machines 
and driers for you to use.

00:08:08.340 --> 00:08:11.420
Lights out is at ten, 
and breakfast is at seven.

00:08:11.420 --> 00:08:13.070
Oh, and the curfew is nine.

00:08:13.070 --> 00:08:15.030
If you're going to be late because 
of school-related activities,

00:08:15.030 --> 00:08:16.680
let them know by seven.

00:08:16.680 --> 00:08:17.600
I see.

00:08:18.060 --> 00:08:20.540
You can read about the details 
in a file called "Dorm Rules"

00:08:20.540 --> 00:08:22.600
on the PC in your room.

00:08:22.960 --> 00:08:24.980
I see. Got it.

00:08:37.010 --> 00:08:39.980
There's still some time before dinner.

00:08:44.820 --> 00:08:47.750
Tachibana-kun, this was fantastic.

00:08:49.750 --> 00:08:54.260
Your report moved me.

00:08:54.260 --> 00:08:56.780
P-President, we mustn't.

00:08:56.780 --> 00:08:58.510
I'm the vice president.

00:09:00.020 --> 00:09:02.020
We have to draw the line somewhere.

00:09:04.530 --> 00:09:05.810
It was a dream, huh?

00:09:08.410 --> 00:09:09.770
You're defenseless.

00:09:14.130 --> 00:09:16.280
What's going on?!

00:09:18.780 --> 00:09:21.490
In your room, huh?

00:09:21.990 --> 00:09:23.290
Really?

00:09:23.290 --> 00:09:25.670
I can't believe he dragged 
Ai Ai into his room.

00:09:25.940 --> 00:09:26.790
"Ai Ai"?

00:09:26.790 --> 00:09:28.300
He's a predator.

00:09:28.580 --> 00:09:29.590
The worst.

00:09:29.590 --> 00:09:32.080
Ai Ai, you'd better 
stay away from him.

00:09:32.080 --> 00:09:32.800
"Ai Ai"?

00:09:32.800 --> 00:09:35.370
Since she just arrived and 
doesn't know the rules yet,

00:09:35.370 --> 00:09:37.430
she's not being punished.

00:09:37.720 --> 00:09:40.840
At least you only have 
to write an apology.

00:09:40.840 --> 00:09:42.030
Yeah, I guess.

00:09:44.310 --> 00:09:45.720
There.

00:09:46.200 --> 00:09:48.450
You're going 
back to your room already?

00:09:49.170 --> 00:09:52.070
It's time for my 
never-ending adventure.

00:09:52.540 --> 00:09:54.820
You've really gotten into it.

00:09:55.360 --> 00:09:57.600
I'll join you, once the meet is over.

00:09:57.600 --> 00:09:58.530
Sure.

00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:08.260
Why don't we throw a welcoming 
party for you after a bath?

00:10:08.260 --> 00:10:10.580
Don't worry about me. Excuse me.

00:10:10.910 --> 00:10:13.140
Is it all right if we 
stop by Ai Ai's room later?

00:10:13.140 --> 00:10:14.550
Why not?

00:10:14.880 --> 00:10:15.960
All right!

00:10:16.320 --> 00:10:17.700
Excuse me.

00:10:18.180 --> 00:10:19.570
See you later.

00:10:21.020 --> 00:10:23.970
Who is Ai Ai?

00:10:24.320 --> 00:10:26.170
Suzuki-san is kind of...

00:10:26.170 --> 00:10:27.980
...mysterious, wouldn't you say?

00:10:28.300 --> 00:10:29.360
She sure is.

00:10:29.700 --> 00:10:32.160
By the way, could I join 
your welcoming party?

00:10:32.480 --> 00:10:34.230
Absolutely not!

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:52.250
All right. Maybe I'll 
try to level up today.

00:11:00.220 --> 00:11:01.230
Hey.

00:11:01.560 --> 00:11:03.020
You're late.

00:11:03.880 --> 00:11:05.600
I had some real life 
stuff to take care of.

00:11:05.960 --> 00:11:08.100
I had a bunch of stuff to do.

00:11:10.350 --> 00:11:12.220
Ai Ai.

00:11:13.220 --> 00:11:15.110
Did she already go to bed?

00:11:17.440 --> 00:11:22.030
<b>[Darker]
The collective term for the largest enemy force in "PSO2." There are various types, but all of them have a black body and a red core. They show up on planets with life and civilization, and look to bring them to ruin.</b>

00:11:22.030 --> 00:11:26.660
<b>[Solo Player]
Refers to those who play online games alone. Divided into those who don't enjoy the company of others, and those who lack communication skills. The latter are usually called "forever alone."</b>

00:11:28.580 --> 00:11:31.160
Man, that was a perfect clear.

00:11:31.480 --> 00:11:34.320
Honestly, I think I'm doing 
pretty well again today.

00:11:34.320 --> 00:11:35.370
Itsuki!

00:11:35.920 --> 00:11:37.920
You're a failure of an ARKS!

00:11:39.920 --> 00:11:42.710
You were lectured by your friend?

00:11:42.710 --> 00:11:44.930
Yeah, he was super pissed.

00:11:45.360 --> 00:11:46.750
What did you do?

00:11:46.750 --> 00:11:50.680
Well, I was trying to level up,

00:11:51.210 --> 00:11:54.690
so I took down all the Darkers 
I saw, one after another.

00:11:55.080 --> 00:11:57.300
You didn't take any damage?

00:11:57.300 --> 00:11:58.160
I did.

00:11:58.160 --> 00:12:00.310
But I was making great progress.

00:12:00.310 --> 00:12:02.700
I was surrounded by enemies.

00:12:03.050 --> 00:12:04.670
What level are you?

00:12:04.670 --> 00:12:05.730
Fifteen.

00:12:06.020 --> 00:12:07.700
What was the guy in your party doing?

00:12:08.110 --> 00:12:10.230
He was behind me the whole time.

00:12:10.230 --> 00:12:12.840
Aha. No wonder he got mad at you.

00:12:12.840 --> 00:12:14.210
What? Why?

00:12:14.930 --> 00:12:15.710
Listen up.

00:12:16.330 --> 00:12:21.400
In <i>PSO2</i>, unless you develop a character
with extremely high defense,

00:12:21.400 --> 00:12:25.090
you have to block or 
dodge enemy attacks.

00:12:25.090 --> 00:12:27.220
SORO said the same thing.

00:12:27.690 --> 00:12:28.680
SORO?

00:12:28.680 --> 00:12:33.430
Wait. Your friend is S-O-R-O SORO?

00:12:33.430 --> 00:12:34.740
You know him?

00:12:35.170 --> 00:12:39.230
Dude, SORO is a super-famous 
high-level solo player.

00:12:39.530 --> 00:12:41.230
"High-level"? "Solo"?

00:12:41.570 --> 00:12:44.670
"Solo" means he doesn't 
group with anyone.

00:12:44.950 --> 00:12:48.990
Among the ARKS, he's known as 
Mr. Aloof, the Aloof Warrior.

00:12:48.990 --> 00:12:51.460
Why would he team up with me?

00:12:51.790 --> 00:12:53.500
That's what I'd like to know.

00:12:53.810 --> 00:12:55.890
But I do know this.

00:12:56.330 --> 00:13:00.720
SORO fell back to the rear
 so he could support you.

00:13:00.990 --> 00:13:02.010
"Support"?

00:13:02.290 --> 00:13:06.030
It means using healing items 
on you when your HP gets low

00:13:06.340 --> 00:13:10.010
or creating cover for you, 
even if you're surrounded.

00:13:10.620 --> 00:13:12.480
I didn't notice at all.

00:13:13.170 --> 00:13:16.020
I just thought I was amazing.

00:13:20.290 --> 00:13:23.150
What? He didn't turn in his report?

00:13:23.510 --> 00:13:25.430
He said he didn't play.

00:13:25.690 --> 00:13:26.660
He couldn't stick to it.

00:13:34.610 --> 00:13:36.470
You look dispirited.

00:13:39.090 --> 00:13:41.750
Is your failure on 
ORACLE bothering you?

00:13:41.750 --> 00:13:42.640
What?

00:13:43.040 --> 00:13:46.170
I heard you talking to 
Kayano Kota on the roof.

00:13:46.490 --> 00:13:47.350
Oh.

00:13:47.350 --> 00:13:50.680
Debts accrued on the battlefield
 can only be repaid on the battlefield.

00:13:51.590 --> 00:13:53.220
You're an ARKS, too?

00:13:53.220 --> 00:13:54.270
I am.

00:13:54.510 --> 00:13:56.060
At all times.

00:13:56.650 --> 00:14:01.090
If you truly are an ARKS, 
don't throw away your own relationships.

00:14:01.770 --> 00:14:05.680
The battle will continue 
with even greater intensity.

00:14:09.110 --> 00:14:10.820
Talk about an exaggeration.

00:14:13.580 --> 00:14:15.080
<b>Online</b>

00:14:13.580 --> 00:14:15.080
<b>Itsuki</b>

00:14:13.580 --> 00:14:15.080
<b>Offline</b>

00:14:19.190 --> 00:14:21.330
Maybe I was too hard on him.

00:14:21.750 --> 00:14:24.830
Many beginners are overenthusiastic.

00:14:24.830 --> 00:14:25.900
That's fine.

00:14:26.210 --> 00:14:30.100
But you're playing haphazardly without 
reflecting on your inexperienced self,

00:14:30.100 --> 00:14:33.530
and paying no heed to the conditions 
of your surroundings or even yourself.

00:14:34.590 --> 00:14:36.470
You're a failure of an ARKS!

00:14:36.900 --> 00:14:39.230
Who cares as long as 
he's enjoying himself?

00:14:41.900 --> 00:14:43.730
You messed up, SORO.

00:14:48.910 --> 00:14:50.990
What? No report today, either?

00:14:52.110 --> 00:14:53.990
You didn't play again yesterday?

00:14:54.290 --> 00:14:55.270
No.

00:14:55.270 --> 00:14:57.090
Tachibana-kun, a minute.

00:14:59.000 --> 00:15:00.290
I'm sorry.

00:15:00.290 --> 00:15:04.500
Yesterday, I fell asleep while 
working on an assignment.

00:15:05.480 --> 00:15:06.480
Listen up!

00:15:09.510 --> 00:15:11.310
<i>Stop lying all the time!</i>

00:15:11.310 --> 00:15:13.710
<i>I know you've been logging in!</i>

00:15:13.710 --> 00:15:15.390
<i>You think I don't know 
anything, don't you?!</i>

00:15:15.390 --> 00:15:17.100
<i>Unfortunately, I can 
see right through you!</i>

00:15:17.100 --> 00:15:19.710
<i>But if I said that, 
you'd know I'm SORO!</i>

00:15:19.710 --> 00:15:22.950
<i>And even though I said those harsh things,
 I wasn't trying to criticize you!</i>

00:15:22.950 --> 00:15:26.110
<i>I'm planning to apologize 
for that as SORO, too!</i>

00:15:26.110 --> 00:15:28.910
<i>But if you won't show yourself,
 I can't apologize!</i>

00:15:28.910 --> 00:15:31.270
<i>I hate this situation! 
I want to clear the air!</i>

00:15:31.270 --> 00:15:33.490
<i>But it'd be even worse 
if he found out I'm SORO!</i>

00:15:33.490 --> 00:15:35.870
<i>Someone tell me what to do here!</i>

00:15:36.660 --> 00:15:37.500
Um...

00:15:37.500 --> 00:15:38.350
What?

00:15:38.350 --> 00:15:40.470
What did you want to discuss?

00:15:42.800 --> 00:15:44.110
It's nothing.

00:15:44.110 --> 00:15:45.500
Excuse me, then.

00:15:48.210 --> 00:15:49.410
<i>It's no use.</i>

00:15:49.410 --> 00:15:52.880
<i>My communication 
skills are too low.</i>

00:16:06.870 --> 00:16:09.110
<i>He's not even logging in today.</i>

00:16:09.110 --> 00:16:11.850
<i>I even said I didn't mean any harm.</i>

00:16:12.130 --> 00:16:14.220
<i>Wait, I haven't told him yet.</i>

00:16:19.490 --> 00:16:20.520
Crap!

00:16:26.390 --> 00:16:29.840
I just spotted Mr. Aloof 
in the hard Forest area.

00:16:30.180 --> 00:16:31.510
Hard Forest?

00:16:31.510 --> 00:16:33.340
What's a veteran player doing there?

00:16:33.800 --> 00:16:35.390
Maybe he changed classes.

00:16:35.390 --> 00:16:37.070
He had a launcher.

00:16:37.070 --> 00:16:38.390
I saw him, too.

00:16:38.390 --> 00:16:41.350
As usual, he was good, but not 
as good as he normally is.

00:16:58.010 --> 00:17:00.000
I don't have time 
to destroy the cage.

00:17:00.450 --> 00:17:01.450
What's that?

00:17:11.660 --> 00:17:12.510
A rockbear!

00:17:12.890 --> 00:17:14.550
Why now?

00:17:15.340 --> 00:17:16.340
Crap!

00:17:39.700 --> 00:17:41.910
Don't! He'll counter you!

00:17:58.020 --> 00:17:59.550
Itsuki, you...

00:18:02.010 --> 00:18:02.720
This is...

00:18:03.130 --> 00:18:05.480
Can you destroy the cage yourself?

00:18:06.440 --> 00:18:08.230
<i>You're</i> worried about me?

00:18:33.390 --> 00:18:34.240
U-Um...

00:18:34.240 --> 00:18:36.260
I'm sorry about the other day.

00:18:36.580 --> 00:18:38.410
No, I'm sorry.

00:18:38.410 --> 00:18:39.910
You fought excellently.

00:18:39.910 --> 00:18:40.510
What?

00:18:41.580 --> 00:18:42.590
Thank you.

00:18:42.940 --> 00:18:45.050
After this, let's enjoy a concert.

00:18:45.350 --> 00:18:46.520
A concert?

00:18:47.370 --> 00:18:51.270
Quests aren't the only way to enjoy <i>PSO2</i>.

00:18:55.670 --> 00:18:59.030
Hey, guys. Thanks for coming.

00:18:59.490 --> 00:19:04.530
I'll sing passionately with my 
entire body and soul again today.

00:19:05.060 --> 00:19:07.500
Brilliantly, intensely, and vividly!

00:19:07.500 --> 00:19:09.630
Get amped with me now.

00:19:09.990 --> 00:19:11.750
It really is a concert.

00:19:23.950 --> 00:19:28.540
Why did you become my friend, SORO?

00:19:28.870 --> 00:19:32.310
Everyone here calls me Aloof.

00:19:32.800 --> 00:19:34.440
No. SORO.

00:19:34.750 --> 00:19:36.570
That's what I'll call you.

00:19:37.530 --> 00:19:38.880
Do as you please.

00:19:48.950 --> 00:19:51.000
<b>PSO2</b> Report
<b>Tachibana Itsuki</b>

00:19:49.250 --> 00:19:50.420
Here's my report.

00:19:51.440 --> 00:19:53.500
Sorry.

00:19:54.060 --> 00:19:55.350
Good work.

00:19:56.730 --> 00:19:57.500
Yes?

00:19:57.500 --> 00:20:00.860
Class 2-B, Suzuki Aika, 
entering the room.

00:20:03.990 --> 00:20:05.480
Suzuki-san?

00:20:09.550 --> 00:20:11.510
Are you Itsuki's superior officer?

00:20:11.770 --> 00:20:12.520
"Superior officer"?

00:20:12.520 --> 00:20:14.030
Who are you?

00:20:14.030 --> 00:20:16.460
Sh-She's an unusual girl who 
just returned from abroad.

00:20:16.460 --> 00:20:17.740
Her overseas experience...

00:20:17.740 --> 00:20:19.030
Shouldn't matter.

00:20:19.320 --> 00:20:20.610
I have a question.

00:20:20.970 --> 00:20:23.150
Why did you choose this 
man to be an ARKS?

00:20:23.560 --> 00:20:25.410
How dare you speak to 
the president that way?

00:20:25.920 --> 00:20:28.160
Because I have something to prove.

00:20:28.160 --> 00:20:29.160
Prove?

00:20:29.160 --> 00:20:33.020
The Ethernet that enabled
 high-speed wireless communication

00:20:33.020 --> 00:20:35.380
has spread throughout the world 
over the past several years,

00:20:35.380 --> 00:20:38.170
marking the advent of what should be 
called a communication revolution.

00:20:38.850 --> 00:20:40.330
The online game <i>PSO2</i>

00:20:40.330 --> 00:20:44.100
that comes pre-installed on the 
next-generation cloud OS "ESC-A"

00:20:44.100 --> 00:20:49.520
has spread explosively, primarily among 
the young, along with the Ethernet.

00:20:50.750 --> 00:20:54.350
<i>PSO2</i> is a symbol of this era 
of communication revolution,

00:20:54.800 --> 00:20:57.690
and the academy is 
considering banning it.

00:20:58.070 --> 00:21:00.610
Involving itself in the 
freedom of students

00:21:00.610 --> 00:21:04.700
who enjoy the game is tantamount to 
interfering with their private lives.

00:21:04.700 --> 00:21:06.320
I simply wish to prove

00:21:06.320 --> 00:21:09.960
that online games don't cause 
students to neglect their studies

00:21:10.350 --> 00:21:13.200
and prevent this tyranny 
under the name of authority.

00:21:14.250 --> 00:21:18.210
So the academy is the Darkers,
 and you're ARKS?

00:21:18.650 --> 00:21:20.920
That's not a great metaphor.

00:21:21.260 --> 00:21:24.170
Are you a fan of <i>PSO2</i>, as well?

00:21:24.170 --> 00:21:28.220
Lately, I've been trying 
a different class,

00:21:28.220 --> 00:21:33.600
but I've mastered the Force, 
Techer, and Bouncer classes.

00:21:35.000 --> 00:21:38.600
I've completed all missions 
in the VR training program.

00:21:40.750 --> 00:21:41.790
Tachibana-kun.

00:21:41.790 --> 00:21:42.790
Yes?

00:21:42.790 --> 00:21:44.650
She's good.

00:21:44.650 --> 00:21:45.360
I see.

00:21:45.360 --> 00:21:50.310
From now on, have her help you
 write your <i>PSO2</i> reports.

00:21:50.310 --> 00:21:51.370
What? But...

00:21:52.470 --> 00:21:56.140
I hereby appoint her a special 
officer of the student council

00:21:56.140 --> 00:21:58.620
and adviser to the vice president.

00:21:58.620 --> 00:22:00.380
What?!

00:22:01.090 --> 00:22:02.880
I'm counting on you, Suzuki-san.

00:22:03.420 --> 00:22:04.630
Got it.

00:22:08.110 --> 00:22:09.640
What's going on?

00:23:39.680 --> 00:23:41.020
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:23:41.020 --> 00:24:09.120
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:23:42.280 --> 00:23:44.340
SORO-san.

00:23:44.340 --> 00:23:45.440
Whoa, be careful!

00:23:45.740 --> 00:23:47.680
Why did you suddenly hug me?

00:23:47.980 --> 00:23:50.500
What does an ARKS idol want with me?

00:23:50.760 --> 00:23:53.170
That's not much of a reaction.

00:23:53.170 --> 00:23:55.900
Are you really a man?

00:23:55.900 --> 00:23:56.700
What?

00:23:56.990 --> 00:23:58.060
What are you talking about?

00:23:58.060 --> 00:24:00.350
No matter how you look 
at me, I'm clearly a man.

00:24:00.350 --> 00:24:02.700
Why do you think I'm not?

00:24:02.700 --> 00:24:04.440
I don't understand.

00:24:04.440 --> 00:24:08.360
It was just a joke, 
but you seem panicked.

00:24:08.360 --> 00:24:09.170
What?
